at 65,000 tonnes HMS Queen Elizabeth is  the UK's largest ever warship the  aircraft carriers flight deck has an  area equal to 60 tennis courts that's  big enough for four jumbo jets but the  planes lining up on these decks will  have considerably more firepower the  f-35 Joint Strike Fighter is one of the  world's leading jets capable of  supersonic speeds and vertical landings  there's also the fax close-in weapon  system that can fire 3,000 rounds per  minute at incoming enemy aircraft and  missiles a long-range radar can track up  to 1,000 contacts in the air or on the  sea in a 250 mile radius  made by a consortium of defense  companies the ship is the most complex  ever made in the UK it's taken 28  million hours to design and build the  queen elizabeth-class along with a  sister carrier still in construction the  total project is costing over 10 billion  dollars the ship is so massive that  those onboard  each have handheld GPS devices to help  them navigate it one more break from  tradition the Queen will christen the  ship with a bottle of whiskey rather  than champagne in a nod to the ship's  birth in Scotland  Tom Gibson Bloomberg
 

